# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_routes_redos.py" "ROUTES REDOS GATE: PASS" "routes redos + symlink" "cross-tier ROUTE extractor is ReDoS-safe + does not read symlinked files (parser/fuzzing audit). P1 (HIGH, MEASURED ~46s): _HAPI_ROUTE was r'\\.route\\s*\\(\\s*[\\[{].*?path\\s*:...' with re.S — the .*? under DOTALL bridges each .route([/.route({ start to a distant path: across the WHOLE file; extract_route_defs runs it via finditer over every .js/.jsx/.ts/.tsx file (per-file cap MAX_FILE_BYTES=400KB) on the LIVE ingest path (build_graph -> _routes_graph -> scan_repo). A file of .route({ x 50000 (==400KB) has 50000 starts with NO following path:, each re-scanning to EOF -> O(N^2): MEASURED 45.5s; a few such files hang the single ingest/co-change worker for minutes, stalling EVERY tenant's deliveries + the durable inbox. FIX: cap the gap + drop re.S -> [^}]{0,512}? (brace-bounded, stops at the route object's }) like _cg_schema_orm.py's [^}]{0,512} -> linear (~0.13s) + byte-identical routes on legit input + no longer false-bridges a pathless .route({}) into a later path:. P3 (path-traversal): scan_repo's _walk did NOT skip symlinked FILES, so a checked-out tree with evil.js -> /etc/passwd (reachable from the local CLI: dogfood.sh/watch.py/evaluate.py) would open()/read()/route-scan a host file; FIX = if os.path.islink(full): continue. Proves: (1) the adversarial .route({ x N (==400KB cap) input completes <1s via extract_route_defs (was ~46s) + _HAPI_ROUTE has no re.S; (2) legit single/multi-line/array .route({path:...}) defs preserved + no brace-bridge; (3) an out-of-tree symlinked file is SKIPPED while the real sibling is scanned. Content-free, offline" "cross-tier ROUTE extractor ReDoS + symlink-traversal fix: _HAPI_ROUTE's .*?+re.S span (MEASURED ~46s on a 400KB .route({-spam file, hanging the single ingest worker -> every tenant stalled) is replaced by a brace-bounded [^}]{0,512}? with no re.S (~0.13s, same routes on legit input), and _walk now skips symlinked files (no host-file read from the local-CLI scan path)" 12
